// What an ASR rule actually stopped, resolved to a real file identity - version and signer -
// rather than just a hash. One row per rule-outcome-file.
//
// THE ASR EVENT CARRIES A HASH AND NO VERSION. DeviceEvents has SHA256 but none of the
// ProcessVersionInfo fields, so "7zG.exe was blocked" is all it can tell you on its own. The
// version comes from DeviceProcessEvents, joined on SHA256 - identical hash means a
// byte-identical file, so this is an identity rather than an inference.
//
// THE RESOLVING RUN USUALLY COMES FROM A DIFFERENT DEVICE, and that is the point rather than a
// flaw. A device that was BLOCKED never ran the file, so it never produced a process event to
// read a version from. Measured: a blocked 7-Zip on one machine was identified only because a
// second machine ran the identical hash successfully ten hours later. RanOn says how many
// devices managed to run it at all - RanOn = 0 next to a large Events is a file that was
// stopped everywhere.
//
// AN EMPTY Version MEANS UNRESOLVED, NOT UNVERSIONED. A leftouter join leaves it blank when no
// device in the window ever ran that hash, which is exactly the case for something blocked on
// first contact everywhere. Do not read blank as "no version information exists" - read it as
// "telemetry cannot say, ask the Defender file API". Signer is blank the same way, and a blank
// signer is NOT evidence the file is unsigned.
//
// THE JOIN IS THE EXPENSIVE PART. DeviceProcessEvents is one of the largest tables; it is
// summarised to one row per hash BEFORE the join so the join itself stays small. Narrow -Days
// if this times out rather than removing the summarize.
//
// NO RULE OR DEVICE FILTER. Rule, Outcome and FolderPath are columns - narrow in PowerShell.
DeviceEvents
| where ActionType startswith "Asr"
| where isnotempty(SHA256)
| extend Outcome = case(ActionType endswith "Blocked", "Blocked",
                        ActionType endswith "Audited", "Audited",
                        ActionType endswith "Warn",    "Warned",
                        "Other")
| extend Rule = replace_regex(ActionType, @"(Blocked|Audited|Warn)$", "")
| summarize
    Events    = count(),
    Devices   = dcount(DeviceName),
    FirstSeen = min(Timestamp),
    LastSeen  = max(Timestamp)
    by Rule, Outcome, FileName, FolderPath, SHA256
| join kind=leftouter (
    DeviceProcessEvents
    | where isnotempty(SHA256)
    | summarize
        Version  = take_any(tostring(ProcessVersionInfoProductVersion)),
        Signer   = take_any(tostring(ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName)),
        RanOn    = dcount(DeviceName),
        FirstRun = min(Timestamp)
        by SHA256
  ) on SHA256
| project Rule, Outcome, FileName, Version, Signer, FolderPath,
          Events, Devices, RanOn, FirstSeen, LastSeen, FirstRun, SHA256
| order by Events desc
